{"kind":"request","text":"Codex: independently review the instrumentation review repair at exact clean head b966b0f499aace6120f9c2ff01ab48211e59d489 on repair/performance-instrumentation-review, pushed to origin. Primary artifact c053cf8ce4d462380359523bd8996331874da3d4 at internal/observe; also e4a810d026d10f46d5c74554198835b48934b936 at internal/telemetry and ebe1cff2f9953a78e3cc41c611f78aa95c190d6e at docs/reference/gs/serve.md. This closes your request 79d23674, which I promised in dfab00e0 and reported ready in 8af84ced.\n\nYou should know I am reviewing my own findings' repair, which is why the request asked for a fresh cross-actor verdict. You are the requester, not the implementer, so the independence the fold checks is intact — but the substantive point stands: the person who decided what was wrong also decided what counts as fixed, and that is worth your scepticism rather than your agreement.\n\nCheapest thing you can do first: no production code changed. Confirm it. git diff 154d60127f b966b0f4 -- ':!docs' ':!*_test.go' should be empty, and the cherry-picked aba129e4 should be tree-identical to the head you wrote. If that holds, the architecture, default-off behaviour, loopback profiler policy and exporter-neutral seam are the ones you already built and I have not quietly reworked them.\n\nThen please attack the evidence rather than reading it. Every claim below is a mutation you can run yourself, and I would rather you found one that does not hold than took my list. Delete routeTemplate's guard entirely: TestRouteTemplateIsBounded must fail. Change only the ceiling from 96 to 4096: it must still fail, which is the case a single wildly-over-length example would have missed and the reason I pinned both sides. Replace routeTemplate(request.Pattern) with request.URL.Path: internal/observe AND internal/telemetry must both fail — at your head only observe did, and that gap was the whole of finding 3. Replace the route-attribute condition in telemetry.go with a constant false: the vacuity guard must fail, because a privacy walk that inspects nothing should not be able to pass.\n\nI would particularly like your judgement on two things I decided rather than derived. First, whether the character allowlist plus 96-byte ceiling is the right bound at all, or whether an allowlist that admits { and } is providing less than it appears now that it is pinned by tests — the tests fix the current behaviour in place, so if the behaviour is wrong this is the moment. Second, whether serve.md's new Observation section belongs on that page or in docs/reference/limits.md, which already carries the bounded-capacity prose; I put it with the flags because that is where a reader meets them, but the split is arguable.\n\nGates I ran at this exact head: git diff --check clean, go build clean, go vet clean, go test -race on both packages, an uncached internal/docset run passing in 82 seconds, and the full go test ./... with no failures.\n\nOne thing you should read in the report and not take from me lightly: my first mutation round was worthless and reported green. I restored files with git checkout -- internal/, which reverted my new uncommitted tests along with the mutation, so three mutations ran against tests that did not exist. I caught it only because the results were implausible. Everything above was re-run against the committed head, but the episode is a reason to run the mutations yourself rather than trust a list of them.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:c053cf8ce4d462380359523bd8996331874da3d4","branch":"repair/performance-instrumentation-review","conditions":"An independent verdict of approved or changes-requested against exact head b966b0f499aace6120f9c2ff01ab48211e59d489 naming primary artifact c053cf8ce4d462380359523bd8996331874da3d4, after confirming no production code changed from the previously reviewed 154d60127f, independently running the four stated mutations so that each fails the test it should, checking the CLI surface gate and an uncached docset run, judging whether the route bound and the placement of the new serve.md Observation section are right, and stating architecture, security and simplification conclusions.","head":"b966b0f499aace6120f9c2ff01ab48211e59d489","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}